@startuml remote-worker-retire
!theme plain
title Lifecycle of a remote worker (revision 4; variant-aware cleanup and independent state axes): stop, leave and purge on the donor; suspend, retire and revoke on our side; the identity stays pinned unless revoked

actor "Operator (our side)" as OP
participant "Registry / key keeper" as T
participant "swarma-dispatcher + swarma-user-manager\n(project host; account lifecycle)" as D
participant "Bridge (M3) + sshd" as BR
actor "Donor (the machine's owner)" as ADM
participant "curator remote-worker\n(donor bridge role; UID follows variant)" as C
participant "Separate donor provisioner (B only)\n(binary/schema/rules/removal pending; B disabled)" as PH

note over OP, PH
  Independent axes: installation present/purged; donor execution active/stopped/left;
  project workplace admitted/suspended/retired; signing identity pinned/revoked.
  A/C share donor UID; B has separate UIDs. Offline purge proves no remote revocation.
  Stop and revocation marks are persisted BEFORE any process is touched, so a service restart cannot race them.
  User-certificate revocation/expiry never substitutes for closing established sessions and killing jobs.
end note

== donor: stop (pause) ==
ADM -> C: curator remote-worker stop
C -> C: persist "stopped"; end this worker's harness and descendants (never all donor-UID processes); keep the bridge service and the keys; audit line
C --> ADM: stopped (run needs valid admission/credentials/qualification)

== donor: leave (retire the workplace, keep the identity) ==
ADM -> C: curator remote-worker leave
C -> BR: retire request over the channel (if reachable)
C -> C: close the channel; keep K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh and the configuration
C --> ADM: left; "init --rejoin" with a new invitation returns the pinned identity to a newly admitted workplace unless revoked

== project: suspend / retire / revoke ==
OP -> T: suspend: grants paused
OP -> BR: suspend: close sessions; keep workplace
OP -> D: retire workplace
D -> BR: persist channel/grant revocation; stop renewal; user-certificate KRL; close sessions
D -> D: kill every job and its descendants (process group / cgroup); verify no process of the workplace UID remains;\narchive permitted noncredential artifacts only; release account and egress rules
BR -> BR: next frame or envelope from this worker refused (retired); mailbox kept durable
note right of BR: the donor's connection drops; its bridge reports "retired by project" and pauses
OP -> T: revoke (only on compromise or departure): root-signed revocation of K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh
T -> BR: persist revocation; user-certificate KRL; close sessions; stop renewal;\nrevocation record: every frame and envelope from these keys refuses from now on;\na return needs a new key through a new enrolment (rotation is a root-authorized record)

== donor: purge (destroy) ==
ADM -> C: curator remote-worker purge --confirm
C -> BR: report purge; ask revocation outcome (if reachable)
alt channel reachable
  BR --> C: reported workplace and identity states (independent axes; response schema pending)
else channel unreachable
  C -> C: record "channel unreachable; the project side must revoke separately"
end
C -> C: stop owned processes; delete keys, locked config, managed home; retain donor-visible audit
alt A
  C -> C: remove owned user service/artifacts; preserve donor account and unrelated data
else C
  C -> C: remove owned sandbox + user service/artifacts; preserve donor account
else B (future path, disabled while provisioner contract pending)
  C -> PH: remove only B-allocated accounts, egress, sandbox, system service\n(exact closed operation format pending; journal/rollback required)
  PH --> C: removal result
end
C --> ADM: variant-owned artifacts removed; printed revocation result or unknown when unreachable
@enduml
